    },
    {
      "id": "9JoZ4OYYcHwQdyAVkkIym",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 703.8869054793477,
      "y": 13059.433870537161,
      "width": 473,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4I",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2126389046,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1541886283,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788288733999,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Q1. Why does Bash use fork() before exec()?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Q1. Why does Bash use fork() before exec()?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "j0HDHGm3GyPwHp45-U-H2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 747.0448002161897,
      "y": 13090.0876534319,
      "width": 968,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4J",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1463377130,
      "version": 13,
      "versionNonce": 904494309,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788288733999,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Because the parent shell must continue running. fork() creates a child process, and the \nchild calls exec() to replace itself with the requested program.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Because the parent shell must continue running. fork() creates a child process, and the \nchild calls exec() to replace itself with the requested program.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "F3c2Q2Fq6VDeswk0S2lyZ",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 700.593319953033,
      "y": 13199.298179747677,
      "width": 583,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4K",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1421286838,
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 354742251,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788288733999,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Q2. What is the difference between fork() and exec()?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Q2. What is the difference between fork() and exec()?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "dxd8cGTHGu5wWFgo2q5Iw",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 743.8869054793488,
      "y": 13234.170712642415,
      "width": 1034,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4L",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1589059830,
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 1876072517,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788288733999,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "| `fork()`                           | `exec()`                                              |\n| ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| Creates a new process              | Replaces the current process image with a new program |\n| Parent and child continue to exist | No new process is created                             |\n| Child gets a new PID               | PID remains the same                                  |\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "| `fork()`                           | `exec()`                                              |\n| ---------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| Creates a new process              | Replaces the current process image with a new program |\n| Parent and child continue to exist | No new process is created                             |\n| Child gets a new PID               | PID remains the same                                  |\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "wCZ7SzW4PehVuYOjbPSBO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 698.6237475846119,
      "y": 13428.907554747679,
      "width": 319,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4M",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2084865398,
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 511031947,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788288733999,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Q3. What is a Zombie Process?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Q3. What is a Zombie Process?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "aD-c4pB4DbHzhaq6s2Q1H",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 733.2290107425067,
      "y": 13459.433870537152,
      "width": 1122,
      "height": 50,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4N",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1182465386,
      "version": 7,
      "versionNonce": 2025932709,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788288733999,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A zombie is a process that has finished execution but still has an entry in the process table because \nits parent has not yet collected its exit status.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A zombie is a process that has finished execution but still has an entry in the process table because \nits parent has not yet collected its exit status.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "_UPnX1FJLbSc4JAGM4wvH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 697.5711160056642,
      "y": 13573.118081063469,
      "width": 352,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4O",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 302871466,
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 1687433515,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788288733999,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Q4. Why can't you kill a Zombie?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Q4. Why can't you kill a Zombie?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Vxq4hkAMQOJHnpuTbgoD-",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 733.3605896898746,
      "y": 13605.749660010837,
      "width": 979,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4P",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 820413302,
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 48433925,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788288733999,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Because it's already terminated. Only its process table entry remains until it is reaped.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Because it's already terminated. Only its process table entry remains until it is reaped.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "m8YVXyJHw26N41MeJjaGb",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 693.3605896898746,
      "y": 13708.907554747679,
      "width": 473,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4Q",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1726898026,
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 1491784651,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788288733999,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Q5. Difference between SIGTERM and SIGKILL?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Q5. Difference between SIGTERM and SIGKILL?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "PZXkcici6127UKN564BuX",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 721.7816423214535,
      "y": 13745.749660010833,
      "width": 781,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4R",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1660552118,
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 515203685,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788288733999,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "| SIGTERM                         | SIGKILL                           |\n| ------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| Graceful shutdown request       | Immediate termination             |\n| Process can handle or ignore it | Process cannot catch or ignore it |\n| Allows cleanup                  | No cleanup                        |\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "| SIGTERM                         | SIGKILL                           |\n| ------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| Graceful shutdown request       | Immediate termination             |\n| Process can handle or ignore it | Process cannot catch or ignore it |\n| Allows cleanup                  | No cleanup                        |\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "rRRKciUPUWeaccInsd6qx",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 678.6237475846108,
      "y": 13942.591765273966,
      "width": 165,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4S",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2072857450,
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 1536434795,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788288733999,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What is ps -ef?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What is ps -ef?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "xxUdmR7FmIJ4g8IcTHYdu",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 727.3778594267159,
      "y": 13971.345877116073,
      "width": 968,
      "height": 925,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4T",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1335941046,
      "version": 418,
      "versionNonce": 1896205765,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788288733999,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "ps -> only shows current terminal's processes\nps -ef -> entire linux system\n    -e → Show every process on the system.\n    -f → Show the full format (more details).\n\nExample Output\n\n    UID        PID  PPID  C STIME TTY          TIME CMD\n    root         1     0  0 10:00 ?        00:00:03 /usr/lib/systemd/systemd\n    root       701     1  0 10:01 ?        00:00:00 sshd\n    amit      2501   701  0 10:15 pts/0    00:00:00 bash\n    amit      2610  2501  0 10:20 pts/0    00:00:02 python app.py\n    postgres   890     1  0 10:00 ?        00:00:05 postgres\n\nUID ->  Linux administrator started it.\nPID ->  Process ID.\nPPID -> Parent Process ID\nC -> CPU usage (historically the scheduling priority indicator; on many systems it \n    reflects recent CPU utilization). usually 0 , because most process are die\n\nSTIME -> Start time\nTTY -> Terminal associated with the process.\n    pts/0 -> means started from Terminal 0\n    ? -> No interactive Terminal\n    Background services like:\n\n    Docker\n    PostgreSQL\n    Nginx\n        usually shows ?\n\nTIME -> CPU time consumed by the process. 00:00:03 -> \n    The process has actually used 3 seconds of CPU time.\n    Even if it has been running for hours, it may have spent most of that time sleeping.\n\nCMD -> The command that started the process.\n     Example -> python app.py, postgres, systemd",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "ps -> only shows current terminal's processes\nps -ef -> entire linux system\n    -e → Show every process on the system.\n    -f → Show the full format (more details).\n\nExample Output\n\n    UID        PID  PPID  C STIME TTY          TIME CMD\n    root         1     0  0 10:00 ?        00:00:03 /usr/lib/systemd/systemd\n    root       701     1  0 10:01 ?        00:00:00 sshd\n    amit      2501   701  0 10:15 pts/0    00:00:00 bash\n    amit      2610  2501  0 10:20 pts/0    00:00:02 python app.py\n    postgres   890     1  0 10:00 ?        00:00:05 postgres\n\nUID ->  Linux administrator started it.\nPID ->  Process ID.\nPPID -> Parent Process ID\nC -> CPU usage (historically the scheduling priority indicator; on many systems it \n    reflects recent CPU utilization). usually 0 , because most process are die\n\nSTIME -> Start time\nTTY -> Terminal associated with the process.\n    pts/0 -> means started from Terminal 0\n    ? -> No interactive Terminal\n    Background services like:\n\n    Docker\n    PostgreSQL\n    Nginx\n        usually shows ?\n\nTIME -> CPU time consumed by the process. 00:00:03 -> \n    The process has actually used 3 seconds of CPU time.\n    Even if it has been running for hours, it may have spent most of that time sleeping.\n\nCMD -> The command that started the process.\n     Example -> python app.py, postgres, systemd",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "jliacR9_cizbG5PZwqrkg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 698.257793637242,
      "y": 15022.653442905537,
      "width": 451,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
