      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788288897401,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. What is RAM?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. What is RAM?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "p6MYhI0Z169QktA3hyQdd",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 824.6809021898734,
      "y": 5707.274331063432,
      "width": 836,
      "height": 650,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4f",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 422800549,
      "version": 27,
      "versionNonce": 2110908869,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788289043470,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Let's start from the physical machine.\n\nYour computer has:\n    CPU\n     |\n     | communicates with\n     v\n    RAM\n     |\n     v\n    SSD\n\nVery simplified:\n\nSSD → persistent storage\nRAM → working memory\nCPU → executes instructions\n\nSuppose you have:\n\nSSD = 512 GB\nRAM = 16 GB\n\nYour SSD can store hundreds of GB of files.\nBut the CPU doesn't normally execute your application directly from the SSD.\nWhen your application runs, its required code/data are brought into RAM.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Let's start from the physical machine.\n\nYour computer has:\n    CPU\n     |\n     | communicates with\n     v\n    RAM\n     |\n     v\n    SSD\n\nVery simplified:\n\nSSD → persistent storage\nRAM → working memory\nCPU → executes instructions\n\nSuppose you have:\n\nSSD = 512 GB\nRAM = 16 GB\n\nYour SSD can store hundreds of GB of files.\nBut the CPU doesn't normally execute your application directly from the SSD.\nWhen your application runs, its required code/data are brought into RAM.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "P6GrKL2dBlL95T_N8l2D7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 745.5637146898734,
      "y": 6409.399331063432,
      "width": 561,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4g",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1846813669,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 798691845,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788289081536,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2. What happens when our Python application starts?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2. What happens when our Python application starts?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "dPlA-VLJFwg9ZY1tX33dX",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 790.6848084398734,
      "y": 6444.399331063432,
      "width": 363,
      "height": 875,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4h",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 778390699,
      "version": 30,
      "versionNonce": 1480097067,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788289205358,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "python app.py\n\nConceptually:\n\nSSD\n |\n | load required code/data\n v\nRAM\n |\n v\nCPU\n |\n v\nExecute\n\nSuppose our Python process needs:\n\nPython interpreter\napp.py\nvariables\nobjects\nlibraries\nbuffers\netc.\n\nAll of these require memory.\nSo we can think of:\n\nPython Process\n      |\n      v\n    RAM\n\nBut there's an important problem.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "python app.py\n\nConceptually:\n\nSSD\n |\n | load required code/data\n v\nRAM\n |\n v\nCPU\n |\n v\nExecute\n\nSuppose our Python process needs:\n\nPython interpreter\napp.py\nvariables\nobjects\nlibraries\nbuffers\netc.\n\nAll of these require memory.\nSo we can think of:\n\nPython Process\n      |\n      v\n    RAM\n\nBut there's an important problem.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "XfGJMvsT3z2r_JZndzwOn",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 955.5637146898734,
      "y": 6463.399331063432,
      "width": 11,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4i",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 289276971,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 2013489861,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788289151352,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "c_JbbeISHZOyVNAiiUcqH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 735.6379334398734,
      "y": 7395.938393563432,
      "width": 473,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4j",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 659712267,
      "version": 81,
      "versionNonce": 919168325,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788289222178,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "3. Can a Process Directly Use Physical RAM?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "3. Can a Process Directly Use Physical RAM?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "qD3kexQeDF-6dmy8kfDvc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 778.5637146898734,
      "y": 7428.399331063432,
      "width": 539,
      "height": 125,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4k",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1805864805,
      "version": 8,
      "versionNonce": 1490977541,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788289244659,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Not directly.\nThis is one of the most important concepts today.\nA process doesn't normally say:\n\"Give me physical RAM address 0x123456.\"\nInstead, it sees something called Virtual Memory.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Not directly.\nThis is one of the most important concepts today.\nA process doesn't normally say:\n\"Give me physical RAM address 0x123456.\"\nInstead, it sees something called Virtual Memory.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "I8bLXeKae0PCLoH6xNf5Z",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 734.5637146898734,
      "y": 7622.399331063432,
      "width": 187,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4l",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1357761451,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1198278539,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788289252011,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "4. Virtual Memory",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "4. Virtual Memory",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "2phI7W4ARGPm_6wdAtK5G",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 767.8254334398734,
      "y": 7656.395424813432,
      "width": 1045,
      "height": 875,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4m",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1966960837,
      "version": 37,
      "versionNonce": 25642571,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788289394587,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Imagine your machine has: 16 GB RAM\n\nYour Django process might see an address space that looks much larger than the actual physical \nRAM available to it.\n\nFor example:\n\nDjango Process\n\nVirtual Address Space\n────────────────────────\n0x00000000\n      |\n      |\n      |\n      |\n0xFFFFFFFF\n\nThe addresses the process uses are virtual addresses.\nThe operating system and CPU's memory-management hardware translate those virtual addresses \nto physical memory locations.\n\nConceptually:\n\nProcess\n  |\n  | Virtual Address\n  v\nCPU / MMU\n  |\n  | Translation\n  v\nPhysical RAM\n\nThis gives the OS much more control over memory.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Imagine your machine has: 16 GB RAM\n\nYour Django process might see an address space that looks much larger than the actual physical \nRAM available to it.\n\nFor example:\n\nDjango Process\n\nVirtual Address Space\n────────────────────────\n0x00000000\n      |\n      |\n      |\n      |\n0xFFFFFFFF\n\nThe addresses the process uses are virtual addresses.\nThe operating system and CPU's memory-management hardware translate those virtual addresses \nto physical memory locations.\n\nConceptually:\n\nProcess\n  |\n  | Virtual Address\n  v\nCPU / MMU\n  |\n  | Translation\n  v\nPhysical RAM\n\nThis gives the OS much more control over memory.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Yn2BX7syH18Plk8Ok8f0p",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 718.3215271898734,
      "y": 8607.543862313432,
      "width": 363,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4n",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2078033451,
      "version": 25,
      "versionNonce": 1416685163,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788289405528,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "5. Why Do We Need Virtual Memory?",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "5. Why Do We Need Virtual Memory?",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "IcXozwGqjd6mPmX5dsa_B",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 747.5637146898734,
      "y": 8640.278237313432,
      "width": 814,
      "height": 775,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4o",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 3955275,
      "version": 36,
      "versionNonce": 819871691,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788289623869,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "There are several important reasons.\n\nReason 1 — Isolation\nSuppose:\n\nProcess A → Django\nProcess B → PostgreSQL\n\nYou don't want Django to randomly modify PostgreSQL's memory.\nVirtual memory helps provide isolation:\n\nDjango\nVirtual Memory\n     |\n     X\nPostgreSQL memory\n\nEach process gets its own virtual address space.\n\n\nReason 2 — Security\n\nImagine a malicious process trying to access another application's memory.\nThe OS can prevent that through memory protection.\n\nProcess A\n   |\n   X\nProcess B\n\nThis is one of the foundations of process isolation.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "There are several important reasons.\n\nReason 1 — Isolation\nSuppose:\n\nProcess A → Django\nProcess B → PostgreSQL\n\nYou don't want Django to randomly modify PostgreSQL's memory.\nVirtual memory helps provide isolation:\n\nDjango\nVirtual Memory\n     |\n     X\nPostgreSQL memory\n\nEach process gets its own virtual address space.\n\n\nReason 2 — Security\n\nImagine a malicious process trying to access another application's memory.\nThe OS can prevent that through memory protection.\n\nProcess A\n   |\n   X\nProcess B\n\nThis is one of the foundations of process isolation.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "GSA7qbjwCeGUit9U100rp",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 677.5637146898734,
      "y": 9508.399331063432,
      "width": 231,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4p",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 953397163,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 820816779,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788289634211,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "6. Important Question",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "6. Important Question",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "KXRIlStzE3ZDSJon4m0ho",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 718.6848084398734,
      "y": 9533.004799813432,
      "width": 902,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4q",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 430099653,
      "version": 44,
      "versionNonce": 1569678469,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788289755845,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Suppose: RAM = 8 GB\nAnd we run:\n\nProcess A = 4 GB\nProcess B = 4 GB\nProcess C = 4 GB\n\nThat's: 12 GB requested\n\nBut we only have:  8 GB physical RAM\n\nDoes Linux immediately say: \"Impossible!\"\n\nNot necessarily.\n\nThis is where virtual memory, demand paging, page cache, swap, and eventually the \nOOM killer come into play.\nWe'll get to that.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Suppose: RAM = 8 GB\nAnd we run:\n\nProcess A = 4 GB\nProcess B = 4 GB\nProcess C = 4 GB\n\nThat's: 12 GB requested\n\nBut we only have:  8 GB physical RAM\n\nDoes Linux immediately say: \"Impossible!\"\n\nNot necessarily.\n\nThis is where virtual memory, demand paging, page cache, swap, and eventually the \nOOM killer come into play.\nWe'll get to that.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ZbFIKXLw4jWDfOI-6VYEI",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 740.1809021898734,
      "y": 9564.579018563432,
      "width": 11,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b4r",
