      "text": "16. See Processes Using Memory",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "16. See Processes Using Memory",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Fvjmz7Z6xcj-oSWeah7MF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 638.4348084398734,
      "y": 16424.395424813432,
      "width": 506,
      "height": 275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5F",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 329796075,
      "version": 31,
      "versionNonce": 741167877,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788291509091,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "top ->\nYou'll see processes and their memory usage.\nYou can also run:\n\nps aux\n\nLook at:\n\n%MEM. and: RSS\n\nWe'll properly understand these metrics later.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "top ->\nYou'll see processes and their memory usage.\nYou can also run:\n\nps aux\n\nLook at:\n\n%MEM. and: RSS\n\nWe'll properly understand these metrics later.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "cwFoZ7YujUCjuCAPHGmMj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 598.5637146898734,
      "y": 16757.399331063432,
      "width": 264,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5G",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1744901413,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1629915973,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788291515885,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "17. The /proc Filesystem",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "17. The /proc Filesystem",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "1zj-t6HhvAHcjKmzrJc9P",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 638.5676209398734,
      "y": 16789.278237313432,
      "width": 682,
      "height": 550,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5H",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 803864427,
      "version": 28,
      "versionNonce": 722414315,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788291566715,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Remember Day 2 when we discussed filesystems?\nLinux has a special filesystem:\n\n/proc\n\nIt exposes information about the running kernel and processes.\nFor example:\n\ncat /proc/meminfo\n\nThis gives detailed memory information.\nYou'll see things such as:\n\nMemTotal\nMemFree\nMemAvailable\nBuffers\nCached\nSwapTotal\nSwapFree\n\nThis is incredibly useful when debugging Linux servers.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Remember Day 2 when we discussed filesystems?\nLinux has a special filesystem:\n\n/proc\n\nIt exposes information about the running kernel and processes.\nFor example:\n\ncat /proc/meminfo\n\nThis gives detailed memory information.\nYou'll see things such as:\n\nMemTotal\nMemFree\nMemAvailable\nBuffers\nCached\nSwapTotal\nSwapFree\n\nThis is incredibly useful when debugging Linux servers.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "RBg_YJdW5klO4SgBenXBz",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 590.5637146898734,
      "y": 17384.399331063432,
      "width": 551.041015625,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5I",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1293610699,
      "version": 4,
      "versionNonce": 1333444267,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788291594000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "18. Very Important: Free Memory ≠ Available Memory",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "18. Very Important: Free Memory ≠ Available Memory",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "7PnLx3e6NffkHGe-DwiLc",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 631.4387146898734,
      "y": 17423.512612313432,
      "width": 847,
      "height": 1100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "#ffc9c9",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b5J",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 949151653,
      "version": 47,
      "versionNonce": 1201006149,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1788291703465,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Suppose: RAM = 16 GB\n\nYou run: free -h\nand see: Free = 1 GB\n\nDon't immediately think:\n\"Only 1 GB RAM is available!\"\nLinux deliberately uses otherwise-unused RAM for things like file/page cache.\nThat's why available is generally more useful than simply looking at free.\nWe'll go deep into this in the next part.\n\nToday's Mental Model\nYou should now have this picture:\n\n                 Linux\n                   │\n             Virtual Memory\n                   │\n        ┌──────────┴──────────┐\n        │                     │\n   Process A              Process B\n   Django                  PostgreSQL\n        │                     │\n   Virtual Memory        Virtual Memory\n        │                     │\n        └──────────┬──────────┘\n                   │\n                Physical\n                  RAM\n                   │\n                  CPU\n\n\nAnd inside a process:\n\nProcess\n│\n├── Code\n├── Data\n├── Heap\n├── Stack\n└── Other mappings\n\nAnd memory is managed in:  Pages",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Suppose: RAM = 16 GB\n\nYou run: free -h\nand see: Free = 1 GB\n\nDon't immediately think:\n\"Only 1 GB RAM is available!\"\nLinux deliberately uses otherwise-unused RAM for things like file/page cache.\nThat's why available is generally more useful than simply looking at free.\nWe'll go deep into this in the next part.\n\nToday's Mental Model\nYou should now have this picture:\n\n                 Linux\n                   │\n             Virtual Memory\n                   │\n        ┌──────────┴──────────┐\n        │                     │\n   Process A              Process B\n   Django                  PostgreSQL\n        │                     │\n   Virtual Memory        Virtual Memory\n        │                     │\n        └──────────┬──────────┘\n                   │\n                Physical\n                  RAM\n                   │\n                  CPU\n\n\nAnd inside a process:\n\nProcess\n│\n├── Code\n├── Data\n├── Heap\n├── Stack\n└── Other mappings\n\nAnd memory is managed in:  Pages",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
